{"title":"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the median from vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to the median from vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. If the lengths of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, then the length of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b9f395290ab339654013bdc16fac5d837f77ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } \\sqrt{17}\\quad \\text{(B) } 4\\quad \\text{(C) } 4\\tfrac{1}{2}\\quad \\text{(D) } 2\\sqrt{5}\\quad \\text{(E) } 4\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"332\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\nlet the midpoint be M,N ( i.e. AM,BN are the medians); connecting MN we know that AB = 2x and MN = x hence apply stewart's theorem in triangle ABC with median MN first and then apply stewart's in triangle BNC with median MN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME\" title=\"1970 AHSME\">1970 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1970 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1970\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a 